  "profile": {
    "personality": "A wary escort whose determination to stop the raiders complicates a moment when negotiation might resume.",
    "achievements": " He questions the merchant about the attacks and tells a rider to shelter if wounded, offering to drive. He also objects when Papirak is referred to disrespectfully. These are actions and reactions in the scene, not a complete earlier history.   When the slasher realizes he faces adventurers and becomes willing to listen, Clive attacks his mind while demanding surrender. The narrator explicitly says this spoils that opening for peace. Vessalia later restores a conversation through persuasion and healing, then silences Clive while negotiating.  The outcome is neither proof that caution was needless nor that negotiation was impossible. The party still obtains a conditional pause in raids. ",
    "relationships": "Travels with Vessalia, Thorn and Velkyn; his disagreement with Vessalia over force becomes part of their attempt to resume a parley."
  },
